Feature: Every public function has an example, and tests say what they cover
  `pubkit doc-coverage` writes each published library's TESTING.md from the
  examples in its docs and the `// covers:` comments in its tests. With
  `--check`, it fails when TESTING.md is stale, a public function has no
  example, or a test names an item that does not exist.

  Scenario: TESTING.md lists each item with its examples and tests
    Given a library "demo" whose public function "twice" has an example and a test that covers it
    When I run pubkit "doc-coverage" "demo"
    Then it succeeds
    And it prints "wrote TESTING.md"
    And "TESTING.md" contains "| `twice` | 1 | `doubles` |"
    And "TESTING.md" contains "Generated by `pubkit doc-coverage`; do not edit."
    When I run pubkit "doc-coverage" "--check" "demo"
    Then it succeeds

  Scenario: A stale TESTING.md fails the check
    Given a library "demo" whose public function "twice" has an example and a test that covers it
    And pubkit "doc-coverage" "demo" has run
    When the file "TESTING.md" reads "edited"
    And I run pubkit "doc-coverage" "--check" "demo"
    Then it fails
    And stderr mentions "TESTING.md is stale"

  Scenario: A public function with no example fails the check
    Given a library "demo" whose public function "twice" has no example
    When I run pubkit "doc-coverage" "--check" "demo"
    Then it fails
    And stderr mentions "`twice` has no example"

  Scenario: A test that covers an item which does not exist fails the check
    Given a library "demo" whose test covers "thrice", which does not exist
    When I run pubkit "doc-coverage" "--check" "demo"
    Then it fails
    And stderr mentions "covers `thrice`, which is not a public item of demo"

  Scenario: A command-line tool has no TESTING.md to keep
    Given a Rust repository whose crate "demo" is only a binary
    When I run pubkit "doc-coverage" "--check" "demo"
    Then it succeeds

  Scenario: A crate that is not here is named
    Given a library "demo" whose public function "twice" has an example and a test that covers it
    When I run pubkit "doc-coverage" "other"
    Then it fails
    And stderr mentions "no crate here named other"
